    "A910-07": "PASS: Complete assigned 51-package finite union covers actual functions/registrations, recursive runtime versus schema config/default/conditions, admitted inputs and outputs/artifacts, grants/secrets and external effects. Shared canonical explanation carries exact caller/store/receiver responsibility; catalogue/schema links are not substituted. Last lint31/94-source residual and ingress/supervisor mechanisms have separate nonauthor successors.",
    "A910-08": "PASS: The package-specific lifecycle union distinguishes Core attempts/checkpoints, durable store/receiver authority, pure parser/projection/read-only work and process/remote ownership. Concurrency, identity/retry, cancel/no-new-cleanup, resume/reconcile, removal and retained-data boundaries are explained; nonapplicability is mechanism-reasoned. State/wait, transport receipt and legacy Redis cutover corrections close the named omissions.",
    "A910-09": "PASS: Every assigned family has source-backed trigger/effect/state/safe-action/retry and successful versus negative flow. Buster outcome versus execution error, cancellation-before-cleanup, fixed parser bounds, optional evaluator and lint raw-output uncertainty were explicitly corrected. Neither a code listing nor an unexecuted happy-path fixture is represented as successful live operation.",
    "A910-12": "PASS: Prior complete semantic 50-README comparisons and package-specific necessary-claim destinations are preserved by exact unchanged source identity; obsolete/contradictory README claims are explicitly rejected. Ops genuinely has no package README. Corrected companion inputs, JUnit, OpenAPI, Redis cutover, quality evaluator and other named transfers are included; not inferred from file diff or counts.",
    "OPL-001": "PASS: Whole all-51 inventory/purpose/function/configuration requirement is covered jointly by actual policy/catalogue/operator-selection set correspondence and the complete recursive package-family explanation union, including all 50 README semantic comparisons. Canonical use/plugins and catalogue are unchanged and link to the guide/reference union. This is a requirement-level Source decision, not automatic promotion from gate IDs or inventory counts."
